From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:23:11 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 45/45] inkling2: fp8 prompt attention keeps the split path's
 bits

With fp8 caches the global prompt kernel copies the raw codes and scales
in two async stages and dequantises each tile to bf16 before its barrier.
The tile values equal tf_ink2_attn8's, so the partials stay bit-identical.
